# Auth guards

Import from `src/modules/auth/` (`decorators`, `optional-jwt.guard`, etc.) — never `identity/`.

| Intent | Pattern |
|--------|---------|
| Authenticated | Default (global `JwtAuthGuard`) |
| No auth | `@Public()` |
| Guest OK | `@Public()` + `@UseGuards(OptionalJwtGuard)` + `@OptionalUser()` |

## Claims

JWT carries `sub`, `email`, `tid`, `role`. The global guard re-checks membership in DB and refreshes role — do not authorize from token `role` alone.

```typescript
import { CurrentUser, Public } from '../auth/decorators';
import { OptionalJwtGuard } from '../auth/optional-jwt.guard';
import { OptionalUser } from '../auth/decorators';
```

Use `@CurrentUser()` when a token is required; `@OptionalUser()` only with `OptionalJwtGuard`.
